@startuml
!theme plain
title Claim-to-Source Verification and Citation Eligibility
actor User
participant "AI Orchestrator" as AI
participant "Claim Extractor" as CLAIM
participant "Source Discovery" as DISC
participant "Source Verification" as VERIFY
participant "Evidence Matcher" as MATCH
database "Source Registry" as REG
participant "Model Provider" as MODEL
participant "Response Renderer" as UI
participant "Audit Service" as AUDIT

User -> AI: Teaching-and-learning request
AI -> MODEL: Produce draft with claim boundaries
MODEL --> AI: Draft response
AI -> CLAIM: Identify factual and high-risk claims
CLAIM --> AI: Claim list and risk labels
loop Each claim requiring support
  AI -> DISC: Search approved external/public and authorised institutional sources
  DISC --> AI: Candidate sources + retrieval evidence
  AI -> VERIFY: Resolve identity, version, authority, rights and freshness
  VERIFY -> REG: Read/write verified source record
  VERIFY --> AI: Verified / partial / failed
  AI -> MATCH: Test whether evidence supports the exact claim
  MATCH --> AI: support strength + locator + evidence hash
  alt verified and adequately supported
    AI -> REG: Create claim-citation relationship
  else unsupported or unverifiable
    AI -> AI: Remove, qualify or label uncertainty
  end
end
AI -> AUDIT: Store verification trace without hidden reasoning
AI -> UI: Render answer + only eligible citations/source cards
UI --> User: Generic useful response with genuine sources where used
@enduml
